
The pmfcmd file for UNIX/Linux is set up to compute a
free energy of activation for a reaction via one job submission:
csh -e pmfcmd >& log &
The Z-matrix in pmfzmat is for the SN2 reaction of Cl- + CH3CH2Cl.
The system is perturbed from the reactants at a Cl...C separation of
5.5 A (lambda = 0) to the transition structure (lambda = 1) in methanol.
The pmfcmd file executes 50 runs of double-wide sampling, so
delta lambda = 0.01.
Each run has 2.5M configurations of equilibration and 4M of averaging.
The pmfpar file specifies use of PDDG/PM3 for the solute energetics
and partial charges, and the chosen solvent is OPLS methanol using
395 molecules from the stored box of 400.
The entire  pmf calculation takes ca. 24 hours on a 2.4 GHz Pentium.

Upon completion, the file pmfmeoh.CSV was generated using the utility pmfdelg
in boss/miscexec. As with the utility sumdelg, each occurrence of
"DeltaG (" is first grepped from the 50 sum files; the resultant
file is renamed delgsum and is the input for pmfdelg.
As summarized in the resultant output file, pmfmeoh.CSV, the computed free
energy of activation is 22.9 kcal/mol.

In separate, prior FEP calculations, the transition structure was determined
to occur at r(Cl...C) = 2.39 +/- 0.01 A. 
The TS was located using TSzmat and TScmd.
The related calculations for nPrCl and iBuCl are in the subdirectories.

This test job was updated on June 13, 2009 by wlj.
